f 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186320710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186369818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186370621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186370630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186377535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186495156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating Improper Integrals With an Unbounded Upper Limit Using Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186492114 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083344 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6dc2621a-77e1-56d9-af63-1917eaa933b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1045 "Improper Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1050 1320.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186083448 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "075e6353-42e9-5465-b0d4-8a611aacb2c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1069 "q-6294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "322fb4b3-6749-5356-82bf-9541f4f0d3ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083837 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2a+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2a+1|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\infty ) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084071 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084071 #edb/ref 1061 1815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084071 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c285e20d-e2ec-53fd-8f92-b4af1eb89c5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084071 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084072 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084072 #edb/ref 1061 1816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084072 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a81991d4-09b6-50b8-916a-56e523699675" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084072 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084083 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084083 #edb/ref 1061 1819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084083 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "733cda70-34ab-5a5f-b160-4a78fdfc6d84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084083 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084084 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084084 #edb/ref 1061 1822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084084 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b91809e-4ecc-558a-907a-e1c63422b0b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084084 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084085 #edb/ref 1061 1823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084085 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d2518448-5280-5591-b5ce-6431c0d8c899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084085 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084302 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084302 #edb/ref 1061 40594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084302 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "10d64a27-17ee-59cd-8ed6-191e04270a7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084302 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084525 #edb/ref 1064 "An **improper integral** is an integral where at least one limit of integration is unbounded. \n\nFor example, the integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int_2^\\infty \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nis an improper integral because the upper limit is unbounded (i.e., is infinite).\n\nThis improper integral can be interpreted as the shaded area under the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$ shown below. \n\n![](images/38/387754335eb4fe9cc1da3994c74d184fb7a76f44d06e7cdd843ecce043fc790f.png)\n\nTo compute an improper integral, we need to compute the limit of the integral as the upper limit approaches infinity. So, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_2^\\infty \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\,\\textrm d x = \\lim_{a\\to\\infty} \\int_2^a \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nTo compute this improper integral, we start by integrating as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{2}^{a}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{-1}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{2}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }([-\\frac{1}{a}]-[-\\frac{1}{2}]) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the limits as $a\\to \\infty{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{a}) & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\int_2^\\infty \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084525 #edb/ref 1065 927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084525 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "07bb29f4-5642-57f0-814e-1aa4cd26e1e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084525 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084527 #edb/ref 1064 "As we've seen, calculating an improper integral involves taking a limit. \n\nWhen computing this limit, we typically have two possible cases:\n\n- If the limit exists, as it has in the previous examples, we say that the integral is **convergent**.\n\n- However, if the limit does not exist or is infinite, we say that the integral is **divergent**.\n\nLet's discuss a concrete example of a divergent improper integral. Consider the following:\n\n$$\nI = \\int_1^\\infty \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nWe can attempt to work out $I$ by integrating over $x\\in[1,a]$ as usual and taking the limit as $a$ tends to positive infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}|x|]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }([\\operatorname{ln}a]-[\\operatorname{ln}1]) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }([\\operatorname{ln}a]-[0]) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}a) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit of $I$ as $a\\rightarrow \\infty$ is infinite. Therefore, the integral $I$ is *divergent*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084527 #edb/ref 1065 930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084527 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7dfef442-a6e1-5446-ac2a-c51aafd1f10c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084527 #edb/ref 1067 "Divergent Improper Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318202 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318202 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318202 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c05ccd85-237f-566b-a79f-e8d9590a5726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318634 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318634 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318634 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318634 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186318202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318634 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "624feba0-3d98-5dfb-b8fe-2f49ece6f4cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186318634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e009094e-338f-5586-9e0b-28bba5f98113" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319371 #edb/ref 1074 "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{8}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{y}^{-8/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{5}{y}^{-5/3}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{y}^{5}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{5}}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{1}^{5}}}) \\\\  & =-3(0-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319868 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319868 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319868 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9f9a0336-53d4-5bf4-982f-e1f8dd06d1ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320316 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320316 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320316 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320316 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186319868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320316 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "484db524-b951-5719-aef0-f5c80cf2155c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350540" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "45df630e-f651-5e97-a712-bb9ab8cb5834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320712 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we substitute $u=2x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=2x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{6}{(2x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{-3}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}] \\\\  & =-(-1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186377618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377615 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "88a03e6d-8814-51d2-8edb-239663fe528e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377616 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377616 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377616 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dd9b6d3c-0057-574c-87f0-e4101749ea2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377617 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377617 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377617 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3737c8d2-a0da-5074-ba6f-697e878e8a8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377618 #edb/ref 1080 "The integral is divergent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186377618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d2c32b1a-b4cd-59d4-99ae-00c65bacae91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175